Lets the core show an agent's page live in a view of the app's, as a tile the user watches it work
in (#4115), through content::SetPageTile. A tile's views take no pointer, cursor, tooltip or drop,
and the wheel only where the core's tile passes it on, to scroll the page and never to swipe through
its history (#4441). They never take the keyboard, and don't tell the page the frame the tile moves
them to, so the page keeps its size and the core scales its layer into the tile. It takes the screen
of the tile's window, as any page does of its window's, so a 2x window has a 2x page. Its select
opens no menu, which would open over the user's window at the tile and take the pointer and keys.
Visibility is untouched: the page draws while the tile is on screen, as one its window shows does. A
hook only: the core decides which pages are tiles.

